--- !u!114 &757765638
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 757765637}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 812e429b0d5d3c840bf8f4f95a2e490c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::KineticEnergy.UI.AimIntroScreen
  bodyText: "AIM CAMERA VARIANTS\n\nThis build contains six aiming cameras. Switch
    with V / D-pad Right (back: C / D-pad Left).\n\nA - First person: the aim view
    you know - you see through the ball.\n\nB - Behind the player: over-the-shoulder,
    the ball stays visible in the corner as a size reference.\n     Q / Right Stick
    Click swaps the shoulder. Adds a small wobble as a parrallax affect as well.\n\nC
    - First person + landing window: A, plus a corner window showing your\n     landing
    spot whenever the cursor itself is off-screen or hidden.\n\nD - Behind player
    + landing window: B plus that same landing window.\n\nE - First person + look
    around: WASD / Right Stick rotates your view without\n     moving the aim. Controller
    energy inputs move to RB (add) / LB (remove).\n\nF - Behind player + look around:
    the same, over the shoulder.\n\nThe feedback form in the pause menu asks which
    variant you preferred.\n\nPress any button to start."
